r': 'other', 'value': 'ConstantIndicator(4)'}], 'expected': 'instanceof CrossedUpIndicatorRule and rule.isSatisfied(1) == true', 'description': 'NumericIndicator yields values [3, 5, 2, 6] (e.g., via a custom Indicator). The series crosses upward over 4 at index\u202f1 (3→5) and again at index\u202f3 (2→6). The rule must report a satisfied crossing at index\u202f1.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'ConstantIndicator(4)'}], 'expected': 'instanceof CrossedUpIndicatorRule and rule.isSatisfied(2) == false', 'description': 'Using the same series as above, at index\u202f2 the NumericIndicator moves from 5 (above 4) to 2 (below 4); no upward crossing occurs, so the rule must be unsatisfied.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'ConstantIndicator(4)'}], 'expected': 'instanceof CrossedUpIndicatorRule and rule.isSatisfied(3) == true', 'description': 'Continuing the same series, at index\u202f3 the value rises from 2 (below 4) to 6 (above 4); the rule must be satisfied again.'}]}, {'group': 'crossedOver(Indicator<Num>) - other indicator decreasing while this stays constant', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'CustomIndicator(values=[6,5,4])'}], 'expected': 'instanceof CrossedUpIndicatorRule and rule.isSatisfied(0) == false', 'description': 'NumericIndicator is a constant 5 (via ConstantIndicator). The other indicator decreases from 6 to 4, never falling below 5, therefore no upward crossing can happen at any index.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'CustomIndicator(values=[6,5,4])'}], 'expected': 'instanceof CrossedUpIndicatorRule and rule.isSatisfied(2) == false', 'description': 'Even at the last index (2) where the other value is 4 (below 5), the crossing condition requires the NumericIndicator to move from below to above the other; since NumericIndicator never moves, the rule stays unsatisfied.'}]}, {'group': 'crossedOver(Indicator<Num>) - other indicator contains NaN (invalid numeric value)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'ConstantIndicator(NaN)'}], 'expected': 'IllegalArgumentException', 'description': 'Passing an indicator that returns Num.NaN should cause the CrossedUpIndicatorRule constructor (or its evaluation) to reject the input and throw an IllegalArgumentException.'}]}, {'group': 'crossedOver(Indicator<Num>) - other indicator with same delegate but distinct instance', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'NumericIndicator.of(originalDelegate)'}], 'expected': 'instanceof CrossedUpIndicatorRule and rule.isSatisfied(any index) == false', 'description': 'Both NumericIndicator instances wrap the same underlying delegate (e.g., ClosePriceIndicator). Since they produce identical values at every index, no upward crossing can occur; the rule must always be unsatisfied.'}]}, {'group': 'crossedOver(Indicator<Num>) - other indicator lagging by one bar (offset series)', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'ShiftedIndicator(shift=1, base=ConstantIndicator(2))'}], 'expected': 'instanceof CrossedUpIndicatorRule and rule.isSatisfied(0) == true', 'description': 'NumericIndicator yields values [1,2,3] (via ConstantIndicator(1) then plus 1 each bar). The other indicator is the same series shifted right by one bar, so at index\u202f0 the other returns null/undefined (treated as below). The NumericIndicator moves from undefined to 1, which is considered an upward crossing, so the rule should be satisfied at index\u202f0.'}, {'input': [{'parameter': 'other', 'value': 'ShiftedIndicator(shift=1, base=ConstantIndicator(2))'}], 'expected': 'instanceof CrossedUpIndicatorRule and rule.isSatisfied(1) == false', 'description': 'At index\u202f1 both series have the same value (2). Since there is no transition from below to above, the rule must be unsatisfied.'}]}]
